achd                 package:AA                      R Documentation

Age and Coronary Heart Disease Data

Description:

     The 'achd' data frame has 100 rows and 2 columns.

     The data set reports age (in years) and presence/absense (1/0) of
     coronary heart disease for 100 subjects.

Usage:

     data(achd)

Format:

     This data frame contains the following columns:

     'age' the age of subjects (in years);

     'disease' the presence/absence of coronary heart disease (as 1/0). 

Source:

     The data were obtained from

     Hosmer, D.W. and Lemeshow, S. (1989).  _Applied Logistic
     Regression_.  Wiley, New York.  Chapter 1.

References:

     Brazzale, A.R., Davison, A.C. and Reid, N. (2007).  _Applied 
     Asymptotics: Case Studies in Small-Sample Statistics_.  Cambridge 
     University Press, Cambridge.  Problem 22.

     Sweeting, T.J. (2005).  On the implementation of local probability
     mathching priors for interest parameters.  _Biometrika_, *92*,
     47-57.

Examples:

     data(achd)
     plot(disease ~ age, data = achd)
     plot(age ~ factor(disease), data = achd)
